{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon","id":986122,"title":"How would you alter World of Darkness from Canon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T07:37:30-07:00","id":986122,"title":"How would you alter World of Darkness from Canon?","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:54:52-07:00","id":986222,"title":"","content":"I love to create crazy mash-ups.<br /> <br /> - I would add the imbued hunters and the demons like &quot;veterans&quot;, not newcomers. They would exit in WoD from lot of time ago.<br /> <br /> - Some ideas from &quot;Kult: lost divinity&quot; like the lictors.<br /> <br /> - Wraith the olvidion splatterpunk style, but epic splatterpunk, in the dark the light of the hope and faith would shine more. Wraiths could kick-ass some monsters like in the videogames &quot;Doom&quot;, &quot;Mortal Kombat&quot;, &quot;Silent Hill&quot;, &quot;The evil within&quot; or &quot;Clive Baker's Jericho&quot;. Survival horror sometimes, and fireworks festival in another times.<br /> <br /> - Faes wouldn't be about &quot;we can't use magic because tinkerbell effect doesn't allow us&quot;. It wouldn't be about crying for the lost innocence but about surviving supernatural menaces. Some faes would be dangerous antagonist because they want punish humanity who &quot;forgot&quot; old pacts (really extortion).<br /> <br /> - Fomorians more linked to fae origin.<br /> <br /> - False garous, the dancers of the skin could become a weaker version of garou killing kinfold and/or banes. For game mechanis would work like fomorians, but background like a mixture of dancers of the skin and the pure tribes from &quot;Werewolf: the forsaken&quot;.<br /> <br /> - About mages, templars wouldn't be &quot;we hate all supernatural creatures because we are too stupy to respect all we can\u00b4t understand or may break Christians' faith&quot;. I dislike &quot;cult of Extasis&quot; because they are too busy with sex and drugs while nuns are helping the poors. Celestial Chorus is too annoying with that new-age ideas.<br /> <br /> - Technocrazy not so united. Confrotantions between agents from different powers, for example West vs Comunism in the Cold War, or French vs British empires in the XIX centurry (and everybody againts Spanish empire in the explorers age).<br /> <br /> - A corebook for ordinary humans, something like &quot;Hunter: the vigil&quot; vs cults of Demons: the fallen. I would add some ideas about factions from &quot;Hunter: the vigil&quot;<br /> <br /> - The society of Leopold wouldn't so ridiculously fanatics, I don't want bores about &quot;that children are faes, they seem to be innocent, but we are going to hunt them because they are supernatural creatures and we want to terminate all no-Christian one&quot;. (Disclaimer: in the real life Church doesn't allow any magic because supernatural phenomenons are by only two sources, or God or Devil, if you try &quot;good magic&quot; really are you opening your door to infernal forces. Other matter is the fantasy worlds where natural laws are different and then pokemon-like creatures with superpowers ,without links to ocultist sources, are possible).<br /> <br /> - Multiverse, uchrony or parallel worlds, for example a post-apocalipse land ruled by Bone Gnawer garous, or a wild Pangea-(James Cameron's) Avatar where feras fight againt alien invaders.<br /> <br /> - A not real world setting, but a mixture of Ravenloft, Kult: lost divinty, Exalted and Scarrend Lands (and nations from 7th Sea?). This could be a out-of-canon sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:33:07-07:00","id":990030,"title":"","content":"I always modify my WoD from canon. The biggest change is that I don't acknowledge or follow the metaplot. My games can best be summed up as &quot;Revised Edition never happened&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, the fan-game Senshi: The Merchandising is canon along with Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game as well. Meanwhile, Kindred of the East and Demon: The Fallen are explicitly non-canon and I'm considering giving Wraith the axe as well, but I'm unsure.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, basically take early 1e and 2e WoD, move it from 1991 to 2016, remove Revised in its entirety and add in Sailor Moon and Street Fighter. There you go, you have a WoD game the way I would run it.<br /> <br /> It's not conventional, but I like it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T14:59:16-07:00","id":990122,"title":"","content":"Replacing the Camarilla with the Maquerade Traditions, a group of multiple ideologies united by a shared set of principles, rules and a need to hide from humanity. Rather than one homogeneous block the 'Camarilla' is now made up of:<br /> <br /> - The Hermetic Order (The Tremere's power center, one of the strictest regions)<br /> - The Mithraic Tradition (The British Isles and N. France as controlled by a recently returned Mithras.)<br /> - The Camarilla (Vanilla Ventrue)<br /> - The Caliphates (Assamite and some other bloodlines and new factions)<br /> - The Cult of Kali (Hindi vampires)<br /> - The Lancea Sanctum (Lasombra Antitribu and Catholic Cainites)<br /> <br /> As well as a few smaller ones. This allows for easier decentralisation of immediate power without weakening the sect and makes the Masquerade somewhat more sustainable IMHO. This also allows for the Camarilla to obfuscate Noddism by throwing the door open to a dozen or more faiths and requiring that their members show them respect. It also allows them to parlay with foreign nations without it stinking of some huge, unsustainable, inexplicable empire of German Agnostics.<br /> <br /> Oh, and removing hunters with magical powers (save True Faith). It just never sat well with my groups that these guys definitively had their own set of powers and rather threw the power balance out of the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:20:36-07:00","id":990136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990122#post990122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cult of Kali (Hindi vampires)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's rather tiresome that Kali is keep being associated with Vampires even though she's not (she's a Goddess not a Vampire) and it's all based on things taken out of context (the only reference she was drinking blood was actually the blood of Raktabjia to prevent them from respawning since every drop of it's blood produces copies of the same demon/asura, that doesn't make her a vampire) and cultural appropriation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:27:38-07:00","id":990137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990136#post990136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it's rather tiresome that Kali is keep being associated with Vampires even though she's not (she's a Goddess not a Vampire) and it's all based on things taken out of context (the only reference she was drinking blood was actually the blood of Raktabjia to prevent them from respawning since every drop of it's blood produces copies of the same demon/asura, that doesn't make her a vampire) and cultural appropriation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Itchy trigger finger much? I never said she was a vampire, nor did I ever draw these parallels. They're a cult based around the acceptance of death and change. In our game universe their origin is complicated but actually revolves around the Goddess Kali saving the world from the machinations of Vampire kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:32:05-07:00","id":990140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990137#post990137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Itchy trigger finger much? I never said she was a vampire, nor did I ever draw these parallels. They're a cult based around the acceptance of death and change.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case then I wouldn't call it &quot;Cult of Kali&quot; then otherwise I don't know why you call it such in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:33:15-07:00","id":990141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In our game universe their origin is complicated but actually revolves around the Goddess Kali saving the world from the machinations of Vampire kind. </div> </div> </div>^ This. See above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:39:28-07:00","id":990143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990137#post990137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our game universe their origin is complicated but actually revolves around the Goddess Kali saving the world from the machinations of Vampire kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm...okay? However although I would figure that Kali has bigger fish to fry like stumping out Asura from her own mythology and destroying negative karma (if I'm positive) or basically doing her daily duties as a Goddess than vampires though...<br /> <br /> Since Kali herself is quite complicated since not only she's the &quot;Goddess of Destruction&quot; but also she's a Cosmic Mother Goddess as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:45:27-07:00","id":990145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990143#post990143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ummm...okay? However though, Kali has bigger fish to fry like stumping out Asura from her own mythology than vampires though...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*sighs* Look, I'm not going to post the documents here, they're enormous, but your complaint is that Kali has bigger things to worry about? Seriously? Isn't that like suggesting vampires can't be Christians because Jesus never mentioned vampirism? And that's discounting the fact that Hinduism is actually an umbrella for dozens of traditions, some of whom are essentially atheists and treat it more as a school of philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:48:28-07:00","id":990147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990145#post990145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sighs* Look, I'm not going to post the documents here, they're enormous, your complaint is that Kali has bigger things to worry about? Seriously? Isn't that like suggesting vampires can't be Christians because Jesus never mentioned vampirism? And that's discounting the fact that Hinduism is actually an umbrella for dozens of schools and traditions, some of whom are essentially atheists and treat it more as a school of philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'm trying to be vanilla to the myths as possible but since this is the WoD however, things can be a little different to fit the context of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:52:30-07:00","id":990150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990147#post990147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I'm trying to be vanilla to the myths as possible but since this is the WoD however, things can be a little different to fit the context of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair enough but I assure you, I've been extremely careful to do a whole lot of homework and story building on this one and, considering the perplexing depth and breadth of Hinduism I'll never take every single facet in to account. I agree that it's irritating when someone takes the cosmetic aspects of a major culture or religion without doing any real research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-19-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T17:02:30-07:00","id":990164,"title":"","content":"I would like the Kindred to have been created as the ultimate weapon against the minions Outer Dark. The Kindred are capable of practically consuming anything, so I think it would be appropriate if they were created to hunt down and consume a greater evil. It may be that they were too successful and, over time, forgot their original purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T17:08:18-07:00","id":990166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/986122-how-would-you-alter-world-of-darkness-from-canon?p=990164#post990164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like the Kindred to have been created as the ultimate weapon against the minions Outer Dark. The Kindred are capable of practically consuming anything, so I think it would be appropriate if they were created to hunt down and consume a greater evil. It may be that they were too successful and, over time, forgot their original purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, this is the mistake Cappadocious made. He planned to diablerise God, he should have diablerised the Storyteller instead.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness my recent campaign has been based around the gnostic apocrypha, especially <i>The Apocalypse of Adam</i>. It takes up the notion that Adam and his family were planning to overthrow God, and were actually capable of it, so God sent down angels posing as Adam to impregnate Eve so that he could control the lineage of Seth. The implication is that now only the lineages of Caine, Lilith and Samael are capable of overthrowing the demiurge and, as with the aforementioned Cappadocious, they're getting closer to that goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-19-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:17:42-07:00","id":990208,"title":"","content":"I only use the original five game lines. I generally accept the corebooks as is, but everything else in supplements might be included, removed, or altered as I like. I ignore metaplot completely so the game is essentially second edition status quo.<br /> <br /> I really have only ever played Vampire and Werewolf, so my changes are basically to those lines. If I were to summarize the major changes, they'd be:<br /> <br /> Vampire:<ul><li>I downplay all the Independent Clans. None are anywhere close to power or numbers of any of the Camarilla Seven although the Setites are the largest. The Giovanni and Assamites are particularly few in number.</li> <li>Many Followers of Set are in the Camarilla or at least claim membership of it, and therefore accept the authority of the Inner Circle and Justicars.</li> <li>I ignore bloodlines entirely unless I am running a plot where one is prominent. Some bloodlines aren't related to the existing vampire genealogies at all, but have their own, modern origin due to curses or other bad juju. This is suspected by the dominant Cainite line which explains why they are persecuted.</li> <li>Camarilla is what is was described in the original books - a worldwide conspiracy of &quot;all&quot; vampires. Vampires don't have different sects based on modern version of multiculturalism. Elders don't care about that, and the idea that the Camarilla are &quot;European vampires&quot; is ridiculous.</li> <li>If the subject is ever brought up, the Elders believe that the rising of Cappadocious from torpor was a historical event and was the origin of the Black Death. This explains why the Camarilla was OK with Cappadocious's destruction by the Giovanni. They believe more pandemics would have happened if he hadn't been destroyed. They don't talk about this much as it contradicts their &quot;antedeluvians are all dead&quot; propaganda. Likewise the Sabbat takes this as more proof they have to destroy the antedeluvians.</li> <li>The Tremere have many enemies outside of the vampires, and this occupies much of their energy. House Tytalus is still trying to destroy them and is major antagonist.</li> </ul><br /> Werewolf:<ul><li>I reduce the number of werewolves out there considerably from canon. I've come to the conclusion they work best in very low populations. Most cities even lack Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers.</li> <li>I use a more Lovecraftian interpretation of the Wyrm as I am often unimpressed with canonical fomori types, Wyrm cults, and PENTEX.</li> <li>&quot;PENTEX&quot; is basically the aliens from They Live trying to anti-terraform the world for their alien masters. Any other elements of canonical PENTEX I like are simply separate corporate conspiracies.</li> <li>I do my best to make werewolves more like they are depicted in traditional media (movies, folklore) rather than the fantasy D&amp;D with ecoterrorism I think canon and many fans treat them as</li> <li>I try to keep the dominant politics in the Garou Nation as being sept based (although since many septs are mono-tribal or with set number of few tribes, tribal politics often works through the septs).</li> <li>I try to make the spirit totems more like they are portrayed in myth and legend (see some of my &quot;heretical thoughts&quot; posts on the werewolf forum)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:03:00-07:00","id":990222,"title":"","content":"The idea of transforming the Earth into a 'wet' greenhouse terrestrial planet for alien colonization is something that I have played with too. In my case, the aliens traveled through the Deep Umbra to the Earth, using their technology to pierce the spiritual quarantine that insulates the Sol System from the rest of the Orion Arm, and have manipulated human development to create a habitable environment for their species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}